# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event seraphine_stand_next
# en: Stand Next to Me
title [da37c9] = 站在我旁边
# en: Seraphine pulls you in front of the long mirror in the east corridor. "Stand there," she says. "No, closer." {~She stares at her own reflection, as if at a stranger.|She looks at herself, then at you, then at herself, and lets out a breath.} "Seers can't see themselves," she says. "Unless someone's standing next to them."
text [a83c98] = 瑟拉芬把你拉到东走廊那面长镜子前。“站那儿，”她说，“不对，再近点。”{~她盯着镜中的自己，像在看一个陌生人。|她看看自己，又看看你，再看看自己，长长地舒了口气。}“预言者看不见自己，”她说，“除非有人站在旁边。”
# en: A girl in a paint-stained smock standing before a tall mirror, pulling another student by the sleeve to stand beside her.
scene [e9ba0f] = 一个穿着沾满颜料罩衫的女孩站在高大的镜子前，拽着另一个学生的袖子让对方站到自己身边。
# en: Stay as long as she needs
opt.left.label [760ac1] = 她要多久就陪多久
# en: {~You stand there until the candles gutter. She looks at herself the whole time, very seriously, and when you finally go, she says, "Thank you. I'm taller than I thought."|You stand beside her a long time. At the end she reaches out and touches the mirror where your shoulders almost meet. "There," she says. "That's what I look like."}
opt.left.say.1 [a48742] = {~你一直站到蜡烛快燃尽。她始终很认真地看着自己，等你终于要走时，她说：“谢谢。我比我以为的高。”|你在她身边站了很久。最后她伸出手，摸了摸镜面上你们肩膀几乎相碰的地方。“就是这样，”她说，“我原来长这样。”}
# en: Ask what she sees
opt.right.label [229a32] = 问她看见了什么
# en: {~"A girl," she says. "Next to someone." She doesn't elaborate. She lets go of your sleeve.|"Half a sentence," she says, and laughs, and won't finish it.}
opt.right.say.1 [d164ef] = {~“一个女孩，”她说，“站在某人旁边。”她没有多说，松开了你的袖子。|“半句话。”她说着笑了，却不肯说完。}

@event seraphine_tomorrow_answer
# en: Tomorrow's Answer
title [6d976a] = 明天的答案
# en: "Yes," Seraphine says, as you pass her in the corridor. You haven't said anything. "Oh," she says. "You haven't asked yet. Tomorrow, then." She looks embarrassed, which is rare. "I slip, sometimes. A day ahead. Someone has to tell me what today is."
text [846be6] = 你在走廊里经过瑟拉芬时，她说：“好。”你什么都还没说。“哦，”她说，“你还没问呢。那就明天吧。”她露出难得的窘态。“我有时会滑出去。提前一天。得有人告诉我今天是哪天。”
# en: A seer answering a question nobody has asked yet, in a corridor, the other student frozen mid-word.
scene [a01256] = 走廊里，一个预言者回答了一个还没人问的问题，另一个学生话说到一半愣住了。
# en: Tell her what today is
opt.left.label [aad3f8] = 告诉她今天是哪天
# en: You tell her: the date, the weather, what's for lunch, what she did yesterday. She listens like it's poetry. "Thursday," she says. "I like Thursday. I'll stay." You wonder what you're going to ask her tomorrow.
opt.left.say.1 [ece441] = 你告诉她：日期、天气、午饭吃什么、她昨天做了什么。她听得像在听诗。“星期四，”她说，“我喜欢星期四。我留下。”你开始好奇自己明天会问她什么。
# en: Ask what you'll ask
opt.right.label [136bb9] = 问你会问什么
# en: "If I tell you," she says, "you won't ask it, and then I'll have answered nothing." She drifts off down the corridor, a day ahead of everyone.
opt.right.say.1 [fe8c77] = “我要是告诉你，”她说，“你就不会问了，那我就什么都没回答。”她沿着走廊飘走了，比所有人都早一天。

@event seraphine_dark_room
# en: The Dark Room
title [d689fb] = 暗室
# en: You find Seraphine in a storeroom with no windows, sitting in the dark. "Everyone's futures are so loud today," she says, without opening her eyes. "Yours is quiet. Could you sit in here? Just so it's quieter."
text [246283] = 你在一间没有窗的储藏室里找到瑟拉芬，她坐在黑暗中。“今天大家的未来都好吵，”她没睁眼，“你的很安静。你能坐进来吗？就为了安静点。”
# en: A storeroom with no windows, a girl sitting on the floor in the dark, a crack of light from the door falling across her face.
scene [1145a0] = 没有窗户的储藏室，一个女孩坐在黑暗的地板上，门缝透进的一线光落在她脸上。
# en: Sit in the dark with her
opt.left.label [7d2a5e] = 陪她坐在黑暗里
# en: {~You sit with her in the dark for an hour. Neither of you says anything. When she finally opens the door, her face is calmer, and she says, "You're the quietest person I know." It sounds like the best compliment she has.|You sit in the dark until the bell. Your notes don't get written. She leans her head on your shoulder at some point, and doesn't explain.}
opt.left.say.1 [01b759] = {~你在黑暗里陪她坐了一个钟头。谁都没说话。她终于推开门时，神情平静了许多，她说：“你是我认识的最安静的人。”听上去这是她能给的最高赞美。|你在黑暗里一直坐到钟响。笔记没写成。不知什么时候她把头靠在了你肩上，也没解释。}
# en: Bring her a candle
opt.right.label [835924] = 给她拿支蜡烛
# en: {~You bring a single candle and set it by the door. "That's better," she says. "One small light. It doesn't shout."|You bring a candle. She watches it as if it were a friend, and the noise goes away, she says, a little.}
opt.right.say.1 [e48328] = {~你拿来一支蜡烛，放在门边。“好多了，”她说，“一小点光。它不嚷嚷。”|你拿来一支蜡烛。她看着它，像看着一个朋友。她说，那些噪声退去了，一点点。}

@event seraphine_already_happened
# en: She Tells You the Ending
title [8077e4] = 她把结局告诉你
# en: You read together now, the two of you, one book between you in the window seat. Seraphine always knows the ending. {~Today she's trying very hard not to say it.|Today she's covering the last page with her hand.} "Don't look ahead," she says. "It's better not knowing. I'm told."
text [c3342c] = 现在你们俩一起读书，窗台上，一本书摊在两人中间。瑟拉芬总是知道结局。{~今天她在拼命忍着不说。|今天她用手捂着最后一页。}“别往后看，”她说，“不知道更好。别人是这么告诉我的。”
# en: Two people curled in a window seat with one book between them, one of them covering the page with her hand.
scene [8e2b8f] = 两个人蜷在窗台上，中间一本书，其中一个用手捂着书页。
# en: Read it slowly, together
opt.left.label [aa3f5e] = 一起慢慢读
# en: {~You read aloud, slowly, one page at a time. She doesn't say the ending. At the end she says, "I was wrong. It ends happier than I saw." It's the first time she's ever been glad to be wrong.|You read and she listens, and twice she starts to say something and stops. When you finish, she's smiling. "I didn't know," she says. "I didn't let myself."}
opt.left.say.1 [1c1504] = {~你出声慢慢地读，一次一页。她没说结局。读完时她说：“我错了。结局比我看见的要快乐。”这是她第一次为自己错了而高兴。|你读，她听，有两次她想说什么又停住了。读完时她在微笑。“我不知道，”她说，“我没让自己知道。”}
# en: Ask her to tell you
opt.right.label [fb782a] = 让她告诉你
# en: {~She tells you the ending, delighted, in half a sentence. You finish the other half together, wrong, and laugh.|She tells you. It's terrible. You read it anyway, and she was right, and you both throw the book across the room.}
opt.right.say.1 [11b507] = {~她兴高采烈地用半句话告诉你结局。另外半句你们一起补完，补错了，笑成一团。|她告诉你了。结局很糟。你们还是读了，她说得没错，你们俩一起把书扔到了房间另一头。}

@event seraphine_dont_look
# en: Don't Look Ahead
title [0be495] = 别往前看
# en: You find a painting under Seraphine's bed: the two of you, older, somewhere you've never been. "I didn't mean to look," she says. "It just came. I'm sorry. I know you didn't want to know."
text [768895] = 你在瑟拉芬床底下发现一幅画：你们俩，年纪大些，在一个你从没去过的地方。“我不是故意看的，”她说，“它自己来的。对不起。我知道你不想知道。”
# en: A seer with paint on her hands looking guilty, another student holding up a canvas that shows them both, older.
scene [9e1e95] = 一个手上沾着颜料的预言者一脸内疚，另一个学生举着一幅画布，画的是年纪大些的她们俩。
# en: "Tell me about it, then."
opt.left.label [a10cc9] = “那就讲给我听。”
# en: She tells you, half a sentence at a time: a house by water, a dog with one ear up, a garden that does badly. "That's all," she says. "That's all I let myself see." You hang the painting where you'll both see it.
opt.left.say.1 [2f1dee] = 她一次半句地讲给你听：水边的一座房子，一只一边耳朵竖着的狗，一个打理得不太好的花园。“就这些，”她说，“我只让自己看了这些。”你把画挂在你们俩都看得见的地方。
# en: "Don't look again. Promise."
opt.right.label [f7844b] = “别再看了。答应我。”
# en: She promises. You can see what it costs her: it's like asking someone not to hear. But she keeps it. The painting goes back under the bed, face down.
opt.right.say.1 [d23781] = 她答应了。你看得出这让她付出了什么：就像让一个人别去听。可她守住了承诺。画回到了床底下，正面朝下。

@event seraphine_vision_hurt
# en: She Won't Let You Go
title [22a3ce] = 她不让你走
# en: Seraphine catches your wrist in the doorway and won't let go. Her face is white. "Not today," she says. "Don't go out today. I saw it. I saw you hurt." She can't say how, or where. Her hands are shaking.
text [b5e766] = 瑟拉芬在门口抓住你的手腕，不肯放开。她脸色煞白。“今天不行，”她说，“今天别出去。我看见了。我看见你受伤。”她说不出是怎么受的伤，在哪里。她的手在发抖。
# en: A girl in a paint-stained smock gripping another student's wrist in a doorway, her face white, refusing to let go.
scene [e5885e] = 门口，一个穿着沾满颜料罩衫的女孩紧紧抓着另一个学生的手腕，脸色煞白，不肯放手。
# en: Stay in, for her
opt.left.label [8c1731] = 为了她，待在屋里
# en: You stay in. Nothing happens, all day. At sunset she lets go of your wrist and sits down, very suddenly, and cries, and doesn't explain whether it was because you stayed or because it was never going to happen. You'll never know. She says that's the point.
opt.left.say.1 [7ace93] = 你待在屋里。一整天什么都没发生。日落时她松开你的手腕，忽然坐下哭了，也没解释是因为你留下了，还是因为那件事本来就不会发生。你永远不会知道。她说，这正是关键。
# en: Go, and come back to prove it
opt.right.label [05abcf] = 出门，再回来证明给她看
# en: You go. You come back with a twisted ankle from a stair that wasn't where it should be. Seraphine looks at it and laughs, horribly relieved. "That's all?" she says. "That's all it was?" She bandages it herself, shaking.
opt.right.say.1 [edcaf2] = 你出去了。回来时扭了脚踝——一级台阶不在它该在的地方。瑟拉芬看着伤处笑了，如释重负得可怕。“就这样？”她说，“就只是这样？”她亲手给你包扎，手还在抖。

@event seraphine_ex
# en: She Painted the Ending
title [9ad74a] = 她画下了结局
# en: Seraphine stops you in the corridor and gives you a small canvas. It's the two of you, walking away from each other down a long hall, both looking back. "I painted it last spring," she says. "Before. I'm sorry. I knew."
text [fa8132] = 瑟拉芬在走廊里拦住你，递给你一幅小画布。画的是你们俩，在一条长廊里背向而行，都在回头。“我去年春天画的，”她说，“在那之前。对不起。我早就知道。”
# en: A girl in a paint-stained smock handing a small canvas to a former lover in a corridor, both careful not to touch hands.
scene [f19952] = 走廊里，一个穿着沾满颜料罩衫的女孩把一幅小画递给昔日的恋人，两人都小心地不碰到对方的手。
# en: Take it, and go
opt.left.label [b89852] = 收下，离开
# en: You take it. You don't hang it. You don't throw it away, either. Some nights you look at it, the two figures looking back.
opt.left.say.1 [cf90d0] = 你收下了。你没挂起来，也没扔掉。有些夜里你会看着它，看那两个回头的人影。
# en: Ask if she painted after
opt.right.label [27164c] = 问她有没有画之后
# en: "After?" She smiles, for the first time in a while. "Two people having tea. Arguing about a book. I don't know when." She tucks the painting under your arm. "Friends, I think. Yes."
opt.right.say.1 [b9db22] = “之后？”她笑了，这是好一阵子以来的第一次。“两个人在喝茶。为一本书争论。我不知道是什么时候。”她把画塞到你胳膊底下。“朋友吧，我想。嗯。”
# en: "I don't look after," she says. "Not with you. Not anymore." She walks away, a day ahead, already gone.
opt.right.say.2 [3d0906] = “我不看之后，”她说，“对你不看。再也不看了。”她走了，早你一天，已经不在了。

@event seraphine_partner_neglect
# en: You Were in a Different Week
title [98faba] = 你在另一周
# en: Seraphine is on the window seat with two cold cups of tea. "I waited," she says. "I thought you were coming on Tuesday. Then I thought I'd slipped a day. Then I thought you'd slipped a week." She almost smiles. "It's hard to tell, with you, lately."
text [abce4e] = 瑟拉芬坐在窗台上，身边两杯凉掉的茶。“我等了，”她说，“我以为你星期二会来。后来我以为是我滑出去了一天。再后来我以为是你滑出去了一周。”她几乎在笑。“最近，跟你在一起，很难分清。”
# en: A seer waiting on a window seat with two cups of tea gone cold, looking up as another student finally arrives.
scene [179799] = 一个预言者坐在窗台上，身边两杯已经凉了的茶，抬头看着终于到来的另一个学生。
# en: Sit, and stay all evening
opt.left.label [ba943e] = 坐下，陪她一整晚
# en: You sit with her and drink the cold tea. She tells you the date three times, to be sure. You stay until the candle's out. It's Thursday. She's sure of it now.
opt.left.say.1 [84dbba] = 你坐下陪她喝凉茶。她把日期说了三遍，确认无误。你一直待到蜡烛燃尽。是星期四。她现在确定了。
# en: "I'm here now, isn't that enough?"
opt.right.label [03be51] = “我现在来了，还不够吗？”
# en: "Now," she says, as if it were a word in a foreign language. She pours out the cold tea and goes, a day ahead of you.
opt.right.say.1 [23ce16] = “现在。”她说，仿佛这是一个外语单词。她倒掉凉茶，走了，早你一天。

@event seraphine_confess_generic
# en: She Already Knew
title [e91972] = 她早就知道
# en: You've rehearsed this. You start to say it. Seraphine holds up her sketchbook: it's this moment, the two of you, drawn weeks ago. "I know," she says gently. "I've known since spring. I just didn't know what I'd say."
text [fb1e68] = 你排练过。你刚开口，瑟拉芬就举起她的速写本：画的正是这一刻，你们俩，几周前画的。“我知道，”她温柔地说，“我从春天就知道了。我只是不知道自己会说什么。”
# en: A seer listening to a confession with a small patient smile, a sketchbook open on her knee showing the very scene.
scene [7ab8a7] = 一个预言者带着耐心的浅笑听着表白，膝上摊开的速写本上画的正是这一幕。
# en: "Well? What do you say?"
opt.left.label [346e14] = “那么？你怎么说？”
# en: She closes the sketchbook. "I didn't let myself look," she says. "I wanted to hear it." Then she kisses you, and for once, she's as surprised as anyone.
opt.left.say.1 [9c6c55] = 她合上速写本。“我没让自己去看，”她说，“我想听你说出来。”然后她吻了你，而这一次，她和所有人一样吃惊。
# en: Let it rest, for now
opt.right.label [ac46ae] = 先放一放
# en: "Then let's not," she says, with relief or disappointment, you can't tell. She tears the drawing out and gives it to you. "For later," she says. "If there's a later."
opt.right.say.1 [f30883] = “那就先不说吧。”她说，是松了口气还是失望，你分辨不出。她把那页画撕下来给你。“留着以后，”她说，“如果有以后。”

@event corvin_lucky_deck
# en: The Lucky Deck
title [680635] = 幸运牌
# en: Corvin deals you a hand from an old deck, soft at the corners and smelling of pipe smoke. {~"Grandfather's," he says. "It really is lucky. Watch."|"Cut," he says. "Any card. It'll be the queen. It's always the queen."} You win, which shouldn't be possible against Corvin.
text [4cc8e5] = 科尔文用一副旧牌给你发了一手，牌角都磨软了，带着烟斗的味道。{~“我祖父的，”他说，“真的很幸运。你看着。”|“切牌，”他说，“随便一张。会是王后。永远是王后。”}你赢了，跟科尔文打牌，这本不该发生。
# en: A lanky student shuffling an old, soft-cornered deck of cards with impossible speed, grinning across a dormitory table.
scene [188bdd] = 一个瘦高的学生以不可思议的速度洗着一副牌角磨软的旧牌，隔着宿舍的桌子咧嘴笑。
# en: Ask about his grandfather
opt.left.label [e2d597] = 问起他的祖父
# en: {~The jokes stop. He tells you about a man who could find a lost thing in any house, and who taught him to shuffle on rainy Sundays. "He'd have liked you, saint," he says. "He liked people who lost honestly."|He talks for an hour, and none of it is a joke. Then he deals again, and cheats outrageously, so you'll know he's fine.}
opt.left.say.1 [52ef2c] = {~玩笑停了。他给你讲一个能在任何房子里找到丢失物件的人，在下雨的星期天教他洗牌。“他会喜欢你的，圣人，”他说，“他喜欢输得光明磊落的人。”|他讲了一个钟头，没有一句是玩笑。然后他重新发牌，明目张胆地出千，好让你知道他没事。}
# en: Play for real stakes
opt.right.label [70fa5b] = 玩真格的
# en: {~You play for coppers. You win, because the deck likes you. Corvin is delighted and furious and asks for a rematch.|You play until midnight and come out four coppers up. "Beginner's luck," he says. "It's the deck. It's cheating for you."}
opt.right.say.1 [885ad9] = {~你们赌铜板。你赢了，因为这副牌喜欢你。科尔文又高兴又气恼，要求再来一局。|你们一直玩到午夜，你赢了四个铜板。“新手运，”他说，“是这副牌。它在替你出千。”}

@event corvin_last_warning
# en: Last Warning
title [433b1d] = 最后警告
# en: Corvin is sitting on the stairs with a letter with a red seal. For once he isn't grinning. "Last warning," he says. "One more detention and they send me home." He folds it very small. "Home isn't a good place, saint. Don't ask."
text [92fea8] = 科尔文坐在楼梯上，手里一封盖着红色火漆的信。他难得没在笑。“最后警告，”他说，“再关一次禁闭，他们就送我回家。”他把信折得很小。“家不是个好地方，圣人。别问。”
# en: A lanky student sitting on a staircase holding an official letter with a red seal, no grin at all.
scene [90d790] = 一个瘦高的学生坐在楼梯上，手里拿着一封盖红色火漆的正式信函，脸上一点笑意都没有。
# en: Promise to keep him out of trouble
opt.left.label [3b792c] = 答应帮他别惹麻烦
# en: "You?" he says. "Keep me out of trouble?" But he looks at you a long time, and the grin comes back, smaller and realer. "Fine. Deal. You're my conscience now. Terrible job. No pay."
opt.left.say.1 [08480a] = “你？”他说，“让我别惹麻烦？”可他看了你很久，那笑又回来了，小一些，真一些。“行。成交。现在你是我的良心了。差事很烂。没工钱。”
# en: Tell him to stop being stupid
opt.right.label [3fb53f] = 叫他别犯傻
# en: "Wow," he says. "Thanks, saint." But he doesn't pick a single lock all month. You know, because you check.
opt.right.say.1 [9f1512] = “哇，”他说，“谢了，圣人。”可他整整一个月一把锁都没撬。你知道，因为你查过。

@event corvin_route_named
# en: A Route Named After You
title [468555] = 以你命名的路线
# en: Corvin unrolls a map of the castle's passages on your floor. One route is in green ink, new. {~"Found it last week," he says. "Kitchens to the roof, no stairs."|"Library to the lake," he says, "in four minutes, if you don't mind a ladder."} At the bottom, he's labelled it with your name. "Every route needs a name," he says, not looking at you.
text [14d956] = 科尔文在你的地板上铺开一张城堡密道图。有一条路线是新画的，用的绿墨水。{~“上周发现的，”他说，“厨房到屋顶，不用爬楼梯。”|“图书馆到湖边，”他说，“四分钟，如果你不介意爬梯子。”}底下，他用你的名字给它标了名。“每条路线都得有个名字。”他说，不看你。
# en: A lanky student unrolling a hand-drawn map of the castle's hidden passages on a dormitory floor, one route inked in a different colour.
scene [697bca] = 一个瘦高的学生在宿舍地板上铺开一张手绘的城堡密道图，有一条路线用不同颜色的墨水画出。
# en: Walk it with him tonight
opt.left.label [6290f4] = 今晚和他走一遍
# en: {~You walk it at midnight. It comes out on the roof, under more stars than you knew the castle had. Corvin doesn't say anything clever. He doesn't need to.|You walk the whole route, bumping shoulders in the narrow parts. At the end he says, "Well? Is it yours?" It is.}
opt.left.say.1 [f6b2d4] = {~你们午夜去走了。路线通到屋顶，头顶的星星比你知道的城堡上空能有的还多。科尔文没说什么俏皮话。他不需要。|你们走完了整条路线，在窄处肩膀撞着肩膀。走到尽头他说：“怎么样？是你的吗？”是的。}
# en: Ask why your name
opt.right.label [7800e2] = 问为什么用你的名字
# en: {~"Because," he says, and then nothing, which from Corvin is a whole speech. He rolls the map up very carefully.|"It's a good name for a route," he says. "Doesn't give anything away." He means the opposite.}
opt.right.say.1 [32de09] = {~“因为。”他说，然后就没了——对科尔文来说，这就是一整篇演讲。他非常小心地把地图卷了起来。|“这名字适合当路线名，”他说，“什么都不透露。”他的意思恰恰相反。}

@event corvin_goat_clause
# en: The Goat Clause
title [c548c8] = 山羊条款
# en: Corvin needs fifteen crowns. He's drawn up a contract, very official, with a clause at the bottom: "In the event of non-payment, the lender shall receive one (1) goat." He's drawn the goat. It's a good goat.
text [1f4d50] = 科尔文需要十五个克朗。他起草了一份合同，非常正式，底下有一条：“如未能偿还，出借人将获得山羊一（1）只。”他把山羊画上了。是只好山羊。
# en: A grinning student holding out a scrawled contract with a drawing of a goat at the bottom, an empty purse in his other hand.
scene [891e2e] = 一个咧嘴笑的学生递出一份潦草的合同，底下画着一只山羊，另一只手里是空钱袋。
# en: Lend it
opt.left.label [c384a5] = 借给他
# en: You sign. He pays you back in three weeks, which is a personal record, and tells you the goat story anyway, because you asked about the clause. The trolls still have it. It runs them now.
opt.left.say.1 [efd5e7] = 你签了字。三周后他就还了钱，创下个人纪录。因为你问起那条条款，他还是把山羊的故事讲了。山羊还在巨魔那儿。现在是它在管着巨魔。
# en: Refuse, for the goat's sake
opt.right.label [aa80d4] = 为了山羊，拒绝
# en: "The goat deserves better," you say. He laughs so hard he has to sit down. Then he finds the fifteen crowns somewhere else, and you decide not to ask where.
opt.right.say.1 [87bd8a] = “那只山羊值得更好的。”你说。他笑得不得不坐下。后来他从别处弄到了十五个克朗，你决定不问是哪儿。

@event corvin_lock_left_open
# en: A Lock Left Open
title [fc8f54] = 留着的一把锁
# en: You've a tradition now: once a month Corvin leaves a lock open somewhere in the castle, a door that's always shut, and a note on it. {~Tonight it's the clock tower: "Up. Bring cake."|Tonight it's the music room: "Play me something bad."} You have to find it first.
text [998967] = 你们现在有个传统：每个月，科尔文在城堡某处留一把锁开着——一扇总是锁着的门——门上留张字条。{~今晚是钟楼：“上来。带蛋糕。”|今晚是音乐室：“给我弹点难听的。”}你得先找到它。
# en: A door in a castle corridor standing slightly ajar at midnight, a note pinned to it in a messy hand.
scene [3f6b5e] = 午夜的城堡走廊里，一扇门虚掩着，门上钉着一张字迹潦草的字条。
# en: Find it, follow it
opt.left.label [1f3c53] = 找到它，跟上去
# en: {~You find it at midnight. He's waiting at the top with a blanket and a cake he definitely didn't buy. You eat it watching the clock's hands move from the wrong side.|You find the door. He's inside, in the dark, playing a terrible tune on a borrowed piano, just for you.}
opt.left.say.1 [052765] = {~午夜你找到了。他在顶上等着，带着一条毯子和一个肯定不是买来的蛋糕。你们边吃边从背面看着钟的指针走动。|你找到那扇门。他在里面，在黑暗中，用一架借来的钢琴弹一支难听的曲子，只弹给你听。}
# en: Leave a lock open for him
opt.right.label [57ef7b] = 也给他留一把锁
# en: {~You pick your first lock, badly, and leave a note: "Your turn." He finds it in ten minutes and is so proud of you he can't speak.|You leave the observatory door open with a note. He finds it, and you, and says you're a terrible influence.}
opt.right.say.1 [01b8c7] = {~你撬了人生第一把锁，撬得很笨，留了张字条：“轮到你了。”他十分钟就找到了，骄傲得说不出话。|你把观星台的门留着，附上一张字条。他找到了门，也找到了你，说你是个坏影响。}

@event corvin_honest_once
# en: Honest for Once
title [ee4b92] = 难得坦白
# en: Corvin has been joking all evening, and it's getting thin. Something's wrong. Every time you ask, he makes another joke, quicker. "It's nothing, saint," he says. "Nothing's ever anything. That's the trick."
text [26697f] = 科尔文整晚都在开玩笑，玩笑越来越薄。有事不对劲。你每问一次，他就更快地再抛出一个笑话。“没什么，圣人，”他说，“什么事都不算事。诀窍就在这儿。”
# en: A lanky student turning away from another, joking with his back turned, his shoulders tense.
scene [1afbc7] = 一个瘦高的学生转过身去，背对着另一个人开着玩笑，肩膀紧绷。
# en: Make him tell you
opt.left.label [9c7bb7] = 让他说出来
# en: He deflects; get past the jokes.
opt.left.hint [278d90] = 他在打岔；越过那些玩笑。
# en: You don't let him off. Eventually the jokes run out, and he tells you: his brother wrote. Wants money. Threatened to come. You sit with him while he says it all, plainly, no jokes. "That's the first time I've said that to anyone," he says.
opt.left.say.1 [3de646] = 你不放过他。玩笑终于用完了，他告诉你：他哥哥写信来了。要钱。威胁说要来。你陪着他把话说完，平平实实，没有玩笑。“这是我第一次跟别人说这些。”他说。
# en: Every question gets a better joke. You end up laughing despite yourself, and he looks relieved and sad at once, and you know you lost.
opt.left.say.2 [9ea63f] = 每个问题都换来一个更好的笑话。最后你自己也忍不住笑了，他看上去既松了口气又很难过，你知道你输了。
# en: Let him joke
opt.right.label [9fc7f3] = 由他开玩笑
# en: You let him joke. You laugh at the good ones. At the end of the night he says, very quietly, "Thanks for not making me." It's honest. For once.
opt.right.say.1 [3ab341] = 你由着他开玩笑，好笑的你就笑。夜深时他很轻地说：“谢谢你没逼我。”这是句实话。难得一次。

@event corvin_brother_again
# en: The Brother, Again
title [e3f2c6] = 又是他哥哥
# en: Corvin's brother is at the castle gate again. This time he isn't asking Corvin for money. He's looking at you. "So this is who you've been spending it on," he says. Corvin steps in front of you without a joke anywhere in him.
text [22ef2b] = 科尔文的哥哥又出现在城堡大门口。这次他不是来找科尔文要钱的。他在看你。“原来钱都花在这人身上了。”他说。科尔文挡到你前面，浑身上下没有一丝玩笑。
# en: A tough older man in a worn coat looming at the castle gate, a lanky student standing in front of another student protectively.
scene [725064] = 一个穿旧外套的强壮男人堵在城堡大门口，一个瘦高的学生护在另一个学生身前。
# en: Stand beside Corvin, not behind
opt.left.label [9ffa73] = 站到科尔文身边，不是身后
# en: You step up beside him. The brother looks at the two of you a long time, then spits, and goes. Corvin shakes for an hour afterwards. "Nobody's ever done that," he says. "Stood next to me."
opt.left.say.1 [5c8e42] = 你走上前，站到他身边。那个哥哥盯着你们俩看了很久，啐了一口，走了。科尔文之后抖了一个钟头。“从没有人这样做过，”他说，“站在我旁边。”
# en: Pay him to go
opt.right.label [af717a] = 给钱让他走
# en: You give the brother everything in your purse. He goes. Corvin is furious with you, and grateful, and furious about being grateful. "Never again," he says. "Promise me." You promise. You'd do it again.
opt.right.say.1 [d0bf37] = 你把钱袋里所有的钱都给了那个哥哥。他走了。科尔文对你又气又感激，又因为感激而更气。“下不为例，”他说，“答应我。”你答应了。你还会再这么做。

@event corvin_ex
# en: New Locks
title [6ad24d] = 新锁
# en: Corvin is changing the lock on his door. It's a very good lock. "Don't take it personally, saint," he says, with a grin that stops before his eyes. "Old habits. Somebody once had a key."
text [57a77b] = 科尔文在换他门上的锁。是把非常好的锁。“别往心里去，圣人，”他说，笑意没到眼睛，“老习惯了。以前有人有钥匙。”
# en: A lanky student kneeling at a dormitory door fitting a new lock, looking up at his ex with a grin that doesn't reach his eyes.
scene [704f16] = 一个瘦高的学生跪在宿舍门前装一把新锁，抬头看着他的前任，笑意没到眼睛。
# en: Leave him to it
opt.left.label [b84f2c] = 由他去
# en: You leave him to it. You hear the lock click behind you, very final, and very well made.
opt.left.say.1 [28dabb] = 你由他去了。你听见身后锁咔嗒一声，非常决绝，做工也非常好。
# en: "It's a good lock."
opt.right.label [ad0899] = “这锁不错。”
# en: He looks up. Then he laughs, a real one. "It's the best lock in the castle," he says. "I'll show you how it works. You'll never get in." It's an invitation, of a kind.
opt.right.say.1 [dcf11f] = 他抬起头，然后笑了，是真的笑。“这是城堡里最好的锁，”他说，“我教你它怎么用。你永远进不来。”这算是一种邀请。
# en: "It is," he says. "Best I've got." He turns back to it. That's the end of the conversation.
opt.right.say.2 [22b0a6] = “是不错，”他说，“我手头最好的。”他转回去继续干活。谈话到此为止。

@event corvin_partner_date
# en: Supper on Someone Else's Roof
title [7340bc] = 别人屋顶上的晚餐
# en: Corvin's idea of a date is supper on a roof you're not allowed on, made of food from a kitchen you're not allowed in. "It's not stealing," he says. "It's redistribution. The cook knows. She likes me."
text [108212] = 科尔文心目中的约会，是在一个你们不准上的屋顶上，吃一顿从一个你们不准进的厨房里弄来的晚餐。“这不叫偷，”他说，“这叫再分配。厨娘知道。她喜欢我。”
# en: Two people sitting on a high castle roof with a stolen picnic between them, the kitchens' chimney smoking behind them.
scene [6d270e] = 两个人坐在城堡高处的屋顶上，中间摆着偷来的野餐，身后厨房的烟囱冒着烟。
# en: Climb up
opt.left.label [2cbf33] = 爬上去
# en: You eat stolen pie on the roof and watch the lake go dark. He points out every window he's ever climbed through. There are a lot.
opt.left.say.1 [9810a0] = 你们在屋顶上吃偷来的馅饼，看湖面一点点暗下去。他把他爬过的每一扇窗户都指给你看。有很多。
# en: Bring the cook along
opt.right.label [77b691] = 把厨娘也叫上
# en: You talk the cook into joining you. She climbs the roof better than either of you and brings better pie. Corvin is thrilled and slightly outclassed.
opt.right.say.1 [6a0426] = 你说动厨娘一起来。她爬屋顶比你们俩都利索，带来的馅饼也更好。科尔文兴奋极了，又有点被比下去。

@event corvin_saint_jibe
# en: "Saint"
title [136318] = “圣人”
# en: Corvin leans across the doorway with one arm. "Here comes the saint," he says, loud enough for the corridor, and then, lower, grinning: "Does it get heavy? Being better than me? Asking for a friend. The friend is me."
text [c4a1d8] = 科尔文用一只胳膊横在门口。“圣人来了，”他说，声音大得整条走廊都听得见，然后压低声音，咧嘴笑着，“累不累啊？比我好？替一个朋友问的。那个朋友就是我。”
# en: A lanky student leaning in a doorway with one arm across it, grinning, while another student stands in front of him with an armful of books.
scene [06d8b7] = 一个瘦高的学生倚在门口，一只胳膊横挡着，咧嘴笑着，另一个学生抱着一摞书站在他面前。
# en: "It does, actually."
opt.left.label [cb6e44] = “其实挺累的。”
# en: The grin goes. He looks at you properly for a second, then takes half your books without asking and carries them to the library. "There," he says. "Lighter." He doesn't call you saint again that week.
opt.left.say.1 [5c43d3] = 笑容没了。他认真地看了你一秒，然后二话不说接过你一半的书，帮你搬到图书馆。“喏，”他说，“轻点了。”那一整周他都没再叫你圣人。
# en: "You'd know, sinner."
opt.right.label [9411cd] = “你最清楚了，罪人。”
# en: He laughs so hard he has to let go of the doorway. "Sinner," he repeats, delighted, as if you've given him a title. By dinner he's signing his notes with it.
opt.right.say.1 [9cfc1e] = 他笑得扶不住门框。“罪人，”他高兴地重复着，好像你封了他一个头衔。到晚饭时，他的字条都用这个署名了。

@event mir_owl_remembers
# en: The Owl Remembers
title [14b806] = 猫头鹰记得
# en: Mir's clockwork owl lands on your shoulder and hoots. {~"Reminder," it says, in Mir's voice. "Birthday. Yours. In nine days. Do not tell them I remembered."|"Reminder," it says. "Lunch. With them. Wear the green coat." Mir arrives, scarlet, and grabs it.} Mir is mortified. "It's not supposed to say the part in brackets," they say. "Probably. It's a feature."
text [e6300d] = 米尔的发条猫头鹰落在你肩上，咕咕叫了一声。{~“提醒，”它用米尔的声音说，“生日。你的。九天后。别告诉TA我记得。”|“提醒，”它说，“午饭。和TA一起。穿那件绿外套。”米尔满脸通红地冲过来一把抓住它。}米尔窘得要命。“它不该把括号里的话说出来的，”TA说，“大概吧。这是个功能。”
# en: A clockwork owl landing on a student's shoulder and hooting a reminder, its creator running after it in goggles.
scene [daba38] = 一只发条猫头鹰落在一个学生肩上咕咕地报着提醒，它的制造者戴着护目镜追在后面。
# en: Ask what else it remembers
opt.left.label [a351d6] = 问它还记得什么
# en: {~Mir tells you, very fast: deadlines, birthdays, and, slightly, grudges. "And you," the owl adds, unhelpfully. Mir puts it in a bag. The bag hoots your name.|"Everything important," says Mir, and then hears themself, and goes red to the goggles.}
opt.left.say.1 [15dbdf] = {~米尔飞快地告诉你：截止日期、生日，还有一点点，记仇。“还有你。”猫头鹰帮倒忙地补充。米尔把它塞进袋子。袋子里咕咕地叫着你的名字。|“所有重要的事。”米尔说，然后听见了自己说了什么，脸一直红到护目镜。}
# en: Offer to oil its wings
opt.right.label [d62e2c] = 帮它给翅膀上油
# en: {~You oil its wings while Mir explains every gear, with exclamation marks. By the end the owl prefers you, which Mir says is a betrayal and a compliment.|You oil the wings and the owl hoots a perfect C. Mir writes it down: "they fixed the pitch!!!"}
opt.right.say.1 [dde1ad] = {~你给它的翅膀上油，米尔把每个齿轮都讲了一遍，句句带感叹号。到最后猫头鹰更喜欢你了，米尔说这既是背叛也是夸奖。|你给翅膀上了油，猫头鹰咕地叫出一个标准的C音。米尔记下来：“TA把音准修好了！！！”}

@event mir_notebooks
# en: The Notebooks
title [b73d42] = 笔记本
# en: Mir holds out a notebook, one of a stack, battered and bristling with slips of paper. "Three years," they say. "Every idea. Some of them work. Probably. Nobody's read them. You can, if you want. Carefully. Very carefully. With clean hands."
text [261868] = 米尔递出一本笔记本，是一摞里的一本，破旧，夹满了纸条。“三年，”TA说，“每一个点子。有些能用。大概吧。没人读过。你想读的话可以读。小心点。非常小心。手要干净。”
# en: An artificer holding out a battered notebook bristling with paper slips, hesitating, to another student in a workshop.
scene [80f382] = 工坊里，一个奇械师犹豫着把一本夹满纸条的破旧笔记本递给另一个学生。
# en: Read it with them
opt.left.label [425240] = 和TA一起读
# en: You read it at the workbench with Mir hovering, explaining every page before you get to it. Halfway through there's a sketch of you, labelled "test subject (willing?)". Mir pretends it isn't there. You pretend too, badly.
opt.left.say.1 [153ea8] = 你在工作台前读，米尔在旁边转来转去，每一页都抢在你读到之前先解释。读到一半有一张你的素描，标注着“实验对象（自愿？）”。米尔假装它不存在。你也假装，装得很差。
# en: Ask which idea is their favourite
opt.right.label [278e49] = 问TA最喜欢哪个点子
# en: They flip to a page with a drawing of a tiny lantern that remembers who lit it. "This one," they say. "It doesn't work yet. It will." They don't let go of the notebook for the rest of the evening.
opt.right.say.1 [76cb8f] = TA翻到一页，上面画着一盏能记住是谁点亮它的小灯。“这个，”TA说，“它现在还不能用。会能用的。”那一整晚TA都没放下那本笔记本。

@event mir_blueprints
# en: Blueprints
title [bbdb09] = 蓝图
# en: Mir has drawn a blueprint for something for you. {~"A lamp that turns itself off when you fall asleep reading," they say. "Probably."|"A pocket that's bigger inside," they say. "In theory. In practice, it eats keys."} They don't say why they keep making things for you. They hold the blueprint like a confession.
text [74e193] = 米尔给你画了一张蓝图。{~“一盏你看书睡着时会自己熄灭的灯，”TA说，“大概吧。”|“一个里面比外面大的口袋，”TA说，“理论上。实际上，它会吃钥匙。”}TA不说为什么总给你做东西。TA捧着蓝图，像捧着一份告白。
# en: An artificer pinning a blueprint to a workshop wall covered in drawings, all of them labelled with another student's name.
scene [a1c3b7] = 一个奇械师把一张蓝图钉到工坊墙上，墙上贴满的图纸都标着另一个学生的名字。
# en: Help build it
opt.left.label [ff55ff] = 帮忙造出来
# en: {~You build it together, Mir talking the whole time, both of you singed at the fingertips. It works. Mostly. Mir hugs it, then you, then looks horrified at themself.|You build it until midnight. It doesn't work. Mir says that's the best part: now you have to build it again, together.}
opt.left.say.1 [9bd0bd] = {~你们一起把它造出来，米尔全程说个不停，两人的指尖都被燎了。它能用。基本能用。米尔抱了抱它，又抱了抱你，然后被自己吓了一跳。|你们一直造到午夜。它不能用。米尔说这才是最好的部分：现在你们得一起再造一次。}
# en: Pin it up, for later
opt.right.label [4d2c5f] = 先钉起来，以后再说
# en: {~You pin it on your wall, next to your timetable. Mir sees it there the next time they visit and goes very quiet and very pleased.|"Later," you say. Mir nods fast. "Later is good. Later is a plan." They say "later" several times on the way out.}
opt.right.say.1 [c68e5a] = {~你把它钉在墙上，就在课表旁边。米尔下次来时看见了，变得非常安静，也非常高兴。|“以后吧。”你说。米尔飞快地点头。“以后很好。以后是个计划。”出门的路上TA把“以后”说了好几遍。}

@event mir_tinkering_evenings
# en: Tinkering Evenings
title [152cc3] = 修修补补的夜晚
# en: Thursdays are tinkering evenings now. Mir works; you sit on the bench with your feet up, reading or helping or just there. {~Tonight it's a music box that plays backwards.|Tonight it's a kettle that refuses to boil unless asked nicely.} The owl is asleep on a pile of bolts.
text [3cfe9f] = 现在星期四是修修补补的夜晚。米尔干活，你把脚搁在长凳上，看书、帮忙，或者只是待着。{~今晚是一个倒着放的音乐盒。|今晚是一把不客气地问它就不肯烧开的水壶。}猫头鹰在一堆螺栓上睡着了。
# en: Two people at a crowded workbench late at night, one soldering, one reading aloud, a clockwork owl asleep between them.
scene [9f7a0e] = 深夜里，两个人挤在堆满东西的工作台前，一个在焊接，一个在念书，一只发条猫头鹰睡在两人中间。
# en: Hand them the tools
opt.left.label [c9fb16] = 给TA递工具
# en: {~You hand over each tool before they ask. By midnight you know what they need before they do. "You're the best assistant," Mir says, "and the worst distraction." They mean both kindly.|You fetch, hold, steady. The music box plays a waltz backwards and you dance to it, badly, among the bolts.}
opt.left.say.1 [2a9006] = {~TA还没开口，你就把每样工具递了过去。到午夜，你比TA自己还先知道TA要什么。“你是最好的助手，”米尔说，“也是最大的干扰。”两句都是好意。|你递东西、扶着、稳住。音乐盒倒着放起一支华尔兹，你们在螺栓堆里跳了一曲，跳得很糟。}
# en: Read aloud while they work
opt.right.label [f36138] = TA干活时你念书
# en: {~You read them a terrible novel. They laugh at the wrong parts and burn a finger. The kettle boils, eventually, because you asked it nicely.|You read aloud. Mir works slower, listening, and doesn't seem to mind.}
opt.right.say.1 [42687f] = {~你给TA念一本糟糕的小说。TA在不该笑的地方笑，还烫了一根手指。水壶终于烧开了，因为你客气地问了它。|你念出声。米尔干得慢了，在听，看样子并不介意。}

@event mir_not_a_hobby
# en: Not a Hobby
title [249789] = 不是爱好
# en: You said it lightly: "your hobby". Mir has gone very still. "My family calls it that," they say. "A hobby. Something to grow out of. I didn't think you would." They're packing their tools away, carefully, which is how you know they're furious.
text [f44f4d] = 你只是随口一说：“你的爱好”。米尔一下子僵住了。“我家里人就这么叫它，”TA说，“爱好。长大了就会丢掉的东西。我没想到你也会。”TA在收拾工具，非常仔细——你就是从这一点看出TA有多生气。
# en: An artificer furiously packing tools into a case in a workshop, another student standing in the doorway.
scene [334dc0] = 工坊里，一个奇械师愤怒地把工具收进箱子，另一个学生站在门口。
# en: Take it back, properly
opt.left.label [464f6b] = 收回那句话，好好地
# en: You take it back, not with "sorry" but with every thing they've ever made, one by one, and what each one means. By the fifth they've stopped packing. By the tenth they're crying into their goggles. "It's not a hobby," they say. "It's not," you agree.
opt.left.say.1 [f6c4e6] = 你收回了那句话，不是靠“对不起”，而是把TA做过的每一样东西一件件说出来，说清每一件意味着什么。说到第五件，TA不收拾了。说到第十件，TA的眼泪流进了护目镜。“这不是爱好。”TA说。“不是。”你同意。
# en: Ask them to show you what it is, then
opt.right.label [867319] = 那就请TA给你看看它是什么
# en: They stop packing. Then they show you, for three hours, everything, and it's not a hobby. It's a whole life. You never use the word again.
opt.right.say.1 [93b1c4] = TA停下不收拾了。然后TA给你看了三个钟头，所有的一切，它不是爱好。它是一整个人生。你再也没用过那个词。

@event mir_family_summons
# en: The Family Wants Them Home
title [157606] = 家里要TA回去
# en: A letter from Mir's family, on company paper. They want Mir home after this year: the clockworks needs someone, and "play time" is over. Mir is sitting on the workshop floor, very small among their machines. "Probably they're right," they say. They don't sound like they believe it.
text [14159b] = 米尔家里来了封信，用的是公司信纸。他们要米尔今年之后回家：钟表作坊需要人手，“玩耍时间”结束了。米尔坐在工坊地上，在一堆机器中间显得很小。“他们大概是对的。”TA说。听上去TA自己都不信。
# en: An artificer holding a formal letter from a clockworks company, sitting on the floor of a workshop surrounded by half-finished machines.
scene [601761] = 一个奇械师拿着一封钟表公司的正式信函，坐在工坊地上，四周是做了一半的机器。
# en: Help them write back
opt.left.label [7d4c22] = 帮TA回信
# en: You draft it together, all night: what Mir has built, what it's for, what they'll build next. It's the best thing either of you has written. Mir posts it at dawn, shaking. "Whatever they say," they tell you, "I said it."
opt.left.say.1 [9a5da9] = 你们一起起草，写了一整夜：米尔造了什么，用来做什么，接下来要造什么。这是你们俩写过最好的东西。黎明时米尔把它寄了出去，手在发抖。“不管他们说什么，”TA告诉你，“我说出来了。”
# en: Tell them to go and see
opt.right.label [cd9397] = 叫TA回去看看
# en: "Go and look," you say. "Then decide." Mir goes home for a weekend and comes back with a clockwork bird their grandfather made, and a decision they don't tell you yet, and a smile you haven't seen before.
opt.right.say.1 [4e85a7] = “回去看看，”你说，“然后再决定。”米尔回家过了个周末，带回一只TA祖父做的发条鸟，一个还不打算告诉你的决定，和一个你从没见过的笑容。

@event mir_ex
# en: The Owl Holds a Grudge
title [eb0a21] = 猫头鹰记仇
# en: Mir's clockwork owl sees you across the courtyard, lands on a gargoyle and glares. "Grudge," it says, in Mir's voice. "Ongoing." Mir, chasing it, sees you, and stops. "It's not me," they say. "It's the owl. Probably."
text [4a69cf] = 米尔的发条猫头鹰隔着庭院看见了你，落到一座石像鬼上瞪着你。“记仇，”它用米尔的声音说，“进行中。”追过来的米尔看见你，停住了。“不是我，”TA说，“是猫头鹰。大概吧。”
# en: A clockwork owl glaring from a high shelf at a former partner of its maker, ruffling its brass feathers.
scene [c9edb4] = 一只发条猫头鹰在高高的架子上瞪着它主人的前任，抖着黄铜羽毛。
# en: Leave them to the owl
opt.left.label [613796] = 把TA留给猫头鹰
# en: You go. The owl follows you to the library, hooting "grudge" at intervals, until Mir catches it.
opt.left.say.1 [7cbac4] = 你走了。猫头鹰一路跟你到图书馆，隔一会儿就咕一声“记仇”，直到米尔把它抓住。
# en: Offer the owl a gear
opt.right.label [3d230a] = 给猫头鹰一个齿轮
# en: The owl takes the gear and considers it. Then it hoots, quite differently. Mir laughs, surprised. "That's 'acquaintance, improving'," they say. "I didn't know it had that one. I didn't build it in." Maybe it built itself.
opt.right.say.1 [c8b134] = 猫头鹰接过齿轮，琢磨了一下。然后它叫了一声，跟之前完全不同。米尔惊讶地笑了。“那是‘熟人，关系改善中’，”TA说，“我不知道它还有这个。我没装这个。”也许是它自己长出来的。
# en: The owl takes the gear and drops it on your head. "Grudge," it says. "Ongoing." Mir apologises and doesn't.
opt.right.say.2 [495441] = 猫头鹰接过齿轮，丢在你头上。“记仇，”它说，“进行中。”米尔道了歉，又没怎么道歉。

@event mir_gift_given
# en: A Gift With Gears
title [b31fc6] = 带齿轮的礼物
# en: You give Mir a gift. They turn it over three times, then hold it to their ear, then take their goggles off to look at it properly. "It doesn't do anything," they say, wondering. "It's just... for me?"
text [62e881] = 你送了米尔一件礼物。TA翻来覆去看了三遍，又凑到耳边听，最后摘下护目镜好好端详。“它什么都不做，”TA惊奇地说，“它只是……给我的？”
# en: An artificer turning a small gift over and over in their hands, peering at it through goggles as if checking for gears.
scene [cab933] = 一个奇械师把一件小礼物在手里翻来覆去，透过护目镜仔细查看，像在找里面的齿轮。
# en: "It's just for you."
opt.left.label [800918] = “只是给你的。”
# en: They hold it very carefully for the rest of the day, as if it might break, or tick. The next morning there's a small brass gear on your pillow. It doesn't do anything either.
opt.left.say.1 [fca876] = 那一整天TA都捧得小心翼翼，好像它会碎，或者会滴答作响。第二天早上，你枕头上有一个小小的黄铜齿轮。它也什么都不做。
# en: "It could do something, if you made it."
opt.right.label [5a9298] = “你要是改一改，它能做点什么。”
# en: Their eyes light. By Friday it hums, glows, and plays one note when you're nearby. It's not what you gave them. It's better.
opt.right.say.1 [63c8d4] = TA眼睛亮了。到星期五，它会嗡嗡响、会发光，你一靠近就奏一个音。它已经不是你送的那样东西了。它更好。

@event mir_birthday
# en: Not a Birthday
title [820036] = 不是生日
# en: You find out it's Mir's birthday, and turn up at the workshop with a cake. Mir looks at the candle, puzzled. "We don't do birthdays at home," they say. "We do name days. Nobody does mine, but that's the one we do."
text [920d17] = 你得知今天是米尔的生日，带着蛋糕来到工坊。米尔看着蜡烛，一脸困惑。“我们家不过生日，”TA说，“我们过命名日。没人给我过，但我们家过的是那个。”
# en: An artificer at a cluttered workbench, goggles pushed up, looking blankly at a small cake with a single candle set among the springs.
scene [97ea64] = 一个奇械师坐在杂乱的工作台前，护目镜推到额头上，茫然地看着弹簧堆里一块插着一支蜡烛的小蛋糕。
# en: Light the candle anyway
opt.left.label [9c4c32] = 还是点上蜡烛
# en: "Two in a year," Mir says, as you light it. "That's excessive." They blow it out, very carefully, as if it might be a fuse, and then cut the cake with a pair of calipers into exactly equal slices.
opt.left.say.1 [12fddf] = “一年两次，”你点蜡烛时米尔说，“太过分了。”TA小心翼翼地吹灭它，好像那是根引信，然后用卡尺把蛋糕切成分毫不差的几块。
# en: You light it anyway. Mir watches the flame for a while, then blows it out with great precision. "It's a stupid custom," they say, and eat three slices, and save the candle in a drawer of springs.
opt.left.say.2 [86c13f] = 你还是点上了。米尔盯着火苗看了一会儿，然后极其精准地吹灭了它。“这风俗真蠢。”TA说，吃了三块，把蜡烛收进了一抽屉弹簧里。
# en: Ask when the name day is
opt.right.label [806bca] = 问TA命名日是哪天
# en: They tell you, then make you write it down, then check you wrote it down correctly. "You won't remember," they say. "People don't." They say it lightly. They watch you put the note in your pocket.
opt.right.say.1 [288f0e] = TA告诉你，然后让你写下来，再检查你写得对不对。“你不会记得的，”TA说，“没人记得。”TA说得很轻巧。TA看着你把字条放进口袋。
